# =============================================================================
# secrets.map — the single source of truth for credential injection.
#
# Both the CI workflow (.github/workflows/release.yml) and the local deploy
# script (scripts/deploy-local.sh) render .rsc files through scripts/render.sh,
# which reads THIS file. One list, one substitution engine, no drift.
#
# Why that matters: the obvious design is a `sed -e ... -e ...` chain in the
# workflow and a second one in the local script. They diverge the first time
# someone adds a placeholder to only one of them, and the failure is a router
# running a literal "PLACEHOLDER_X" string in production. Keep this file as the
# only place placeholders are listed.
#
# FORMAT (whitespace-separated, 3 columns + free-text description)
#   PLACEHOLDER_TOKEN    ENV_VAR_NAME    yes|no    description
#                                        ^ required?
#
#   required=yes  render.sh aborts if the env var is empty, AND the workflow
#                 refuses to publish assets that still contain the placeholder.
#                 Use for anything the router cannot function without.
#   required==VAL a non-secret SETTING with a default (no spaces in VAL).
#                 Override per router with a GitHub variable or env var of the
#                 same name, or with the same placeholder in the site's own
#                 secrets.map (site lines win over engine lines).
#   required=no   left as the literal placeholder if unset. The scripts detect
#                 the "PLACEHOLDER_" prefix at runtime and disable that feature
#                 quietly. Use for optional integrations.
#
# ADDING A SECRET
#   1. Put PLACEHOLDER_MY_THING in the .rsc file.
#   2. Add a line here.
#   3. gh secret set GITOPS_MY_THING
#   4. Add it to the `env:` block in .github/workflows/release.yml.
#   5. Add it to scripts/.env.example.
#
# NEVER commit a real value to this repo. This file names secrets; it does not
# contain them.
# =============================================================================

# --- Required: the pull agent cannot work without these ----------------------
PLACEHOLDER_GITHUB_REPO       GITOPS_GITHUB_REPO       yes   owner/repo the router polls for releases, e.g. acme/net-config
PLACEHOLDER_GITHUB_PAT        GITOPS_GITHUB_PAT        yes   fine-grained PAT, THIS repo only, Contents:Read. Used by the router to read releases and download assets.

# --- Optional: observability. Unset = feature disabled at runtime. ------------
PLACEHOLDER_LOG_INGEST_URL    GITOPS_LOG_INGEST_URL    no    JSON log sink endpoint (Better Stack / Loki / Elastic / your own)
PLACEHOLDER_LOG_INGEST_TOKEN  GITOPS_LOG_INGEST_TOKEN  no    bearer token for the log sink
PLACEHOLDER_DEADMAN_URL       GITOPS_DEADMAN_URL       no    dead-man's-switch ping URL (healthchecks.io / Cronitor)

# --- Settings (not secret): defaults, override per router --------------------
# Comma-separated hosts the watchdog pings to decide "WAN is up"; ONE reply is
# enough. Do not use a host your router pins to one uplink: a recursive
# check-gateway route like `8.8.8.8/32 via <fiber-gw>` makes 8.8.8.8 unreachable
# while the LTE backup works fine, and the watchdog would roll back a good deploy.
PLACEHOLDER_WAN_PING_TARGETS  GITOPS_WAN_PING_TARGETS  =1.1.1.1,9.9.9.9   watchdog reachability targets

# --- Optional module: modules/capsman/ap-upgrade.rsc --------------------------
# One-shot remote RouterOS upgrade of ONE CAPsMAN AP. Unset = module disables
# itself. See the header of that file and docs/07-ap-upgrade.md.
PLACEHOLDER_AP_UPGRADE_MAC    GITOPS_AP_UPGRADE_MAC    no    variable: AP base-mac AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF
PLACEHOLDER_AP_UPGRADE_RUN    GITOPS_AP_UPGRADE_RUN    no    variable: run id [A-Za-z0-9-], NEW value per run (marker name)
PLACEHOLDER_AP_USER           GITOPS_AP_USER           no    secret: SSH user on the APs
PLACEHOLDER_AP_PASSWORD       GITOPS_AP_PASSWORD       no    secret: its password (no " \ or $)

# --- Optional module: modules/telemetry/telemetry.rsc -------------------------
# WiFi/CAP/LTE telemetry to the log sink above. Unset = every client counts as
# home. See docs/08-telemetry.md.
PLACEHOLDER_TELEMETRY_GUEST_SSID_RE  GITOPS_TELEMETRY_GUEST_SSID_RE  no   variable: RouterOS regex of guest SSIDs (no " \ or $)
PLACEHOLDER_TELEMETRY_WAN2_IFACE   GITOPS_TELEMETRY_WAN2_IFACE   no         variable: backup uplink interface (external LTE box on ethernet); unset = no wan2_* fields
PLACEHOLDER_TELEMETRY_WAN2_GW      GITOPS_TELEMETRY_WAN2_GW      no         variable: gateway to ping on that uplink; unset = from its default route
PLACEHOLDER_TELEMETRY_WAN2_TARGET  GITOPS_TELEMETRY_WAN2_TARGET  =1.1.1.1   variable: internet ping target, used only while the backup uplink is active
PLACEHOLDER_MODEM_FW_MODE         GITOPS_MODEM_FW_MODE         =notify      variable: modules/lte/modem-firmware: notify (report only) or auto (install)
PLACEHOLDER_MODEM_FW_START_DATE   GITOPS_MODEM_FW_START_DATE   =2026-11-28  variable: first weekly run date; its weekday is the run day (2026-11-28 = Saturday)
PLACEHOLDER_MODEM_FW_START_TIME   GITOPS_MODEM_FW_START_TIME   =08:00:00    variable: weekly run time, after the nightly maintenance window
PLACEHOLDER_MODEM_FW_PING_TARGET  GITOPS_MODEM_FW_PING_TARGET  =1.1.1.1     variable: reachability check after a modem firmware upgrade
